In Redux, a component dispatches an action to add an item to a cart. The reducer receives `state = [{id:1}]` and `action = {type:'ADD_ITEM', payload:{id:2}}`. Which reducer implementation is correct?

```js
// A
return state.push(action.payload);

// B
return [...state, action.payload];

// C
state.push(action.payload); return state;

// D
return state.concat(action.payload);
```
